                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web Client",
                "text": "World Mental Health Day is a reminder to check in on our loved ones and know that it\u2019s okay to reach out for support when we need it.\n\nIn southern Ohio, our family farming community works tirelessly day in and day out. They face long hours, geographic isolation, and limited access mental health care. It can be very stressful and often lonely work. I\u2019ve got our farmers\u2019 backs and will continue to advocate not only for their needs to succeed financially, but for their mental health needs as well.\n\nIf you need help, call or text the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline at 988 for free, confidential support.",
